      "id": 1,
      "text": "The original Moro vanished about ten years before the current town was founded.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansasheritage.com/blog/dah/2023/01/20/delta-roads-and-travels---moro"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Because he had grown up in Old Moro, he named the new town Moro.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansasheritage.com/blog/dah/2023/01/20/delta-roads-and-travels---moro"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1907 the Missouri and North Arkansas Railroad announced plans to pass through western Lee County, and the new town was financed and built around that railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansasheritage.com/blog/dah/2023/01/20/delta-roads-and-travels---moro"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Civil War, both armies camped in Moro and the Confederate army that attacked Helena on July 4, 1863, passed through town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansasheritage.com/blog/dah/2023/01/20/delta-roads-and-travels---moro"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Old Moro traces its creation back to 1835 when settlers moved into the region around an intersection.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.arkansasheritage.com/blog/dah/2023/01/20/delta-roads-and-travels---moro"
    },
